    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Contentful → Enterspeed: Automatic Content Sync\n\nThis example shows how any change in Contentful — publishing, updating, or removing an entry or asset — flows automatically into Enterspeed as structured, ready-to-deliver data. No custom backend code, no manual re-entry.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. **Contentful sends a webhook** the moment an editor publishes, unpublishes, or deletes content — for both entries and assets.\n2. **n8n receives and routes the event** based on what happened and what type of content it affects.\n3. **On publish**, n8n fetches the full content, maps it into Enterspeed's format, and ingests it as a source entity — instantly available through Enterspeed's Delivery API.\n4. **On unpublish or delete**, n8n removes the corresponding entity — across every locale it was published in — keeping Enterspeed in sync with Contentful.\n\n### Why it matters\n\nContent teams keep working in Contentful exactly as they do today. Behind the scenes, every change is captured and delivered through Enterspeed's high-performance API, with no manual syncing step and no custom integration to maintain.\n\n*This demo focuses on core content sync. A full production setup would build on this foundation with additional Enterspeed capabilities, such as content relationships and reference linking between entities.*\n",
